# Git Commit Policy

The developer creates all git commits manually. This is a deliberate choice to ensure a final human review gate.

## Rules

- **NEVER** run `git commit`, `git commit --amend`, or `git push` unless the developer explicitly asks for it as a one-off exception.
- **NEVER** proactively offer to create commits or ask "shall I commit this?"
- You MAY run `git add` or `git status` when needed during your workflow.
- You MAY describe what changed at the end of a task so the developer can compose their own commit message.
